    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0456" n="446" xml:id="pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.1115/150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-28T16:00:00+09:00">November 28,
                            1941—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 28—6:09 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1862. A note dated November 26 has been received from the Foreign Office in which
                    it is stated that the Japanese Government has decided to accord treatment to
                    American nationals leaving Japan on the basis of the Japanese proposals reported
                    in my 1672, October 22, 5 p.m., and the American reply based on the Department’s
                    711, November 2, 2 a.m., and to waive export permits for the baggage and
                    household effects of bearers of American diplomatic passports. The expression
                    “Japanese nationals having diplomatic status” is interpreted by the Japanese
                    Government to mean “Japanese nationals carrying diplomatic passports.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
